Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Short Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 3"

	SAY NAME2 "Ilbratha +2"
	SAY DESC "This ancient bronze sword is set with six matching bloodstones and was apparently forged for Azoun the First, a long-dead king of Cormyr. It saw little use and eventually found its way to a favored of the king's guards. Despite the aid of its illusionary magic, that unnamed soldier fell in a later battle, and the sword was lost to brigands or scavengers.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Mirror Image once per day
  Duration: 1 turn

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d6+2 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Short Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 2" 







